  {
    "id": "sitl11-tab",
    "type": "tab",
    "label": "SITL 11 Broadcast vs sequential",
    "disabled": false,
    "info": "Arm five ArduPilot vehicles two ways: sequential fan-out (paced, per-vehicle acks) vs broadcast (target_system=0). Compare aggregates and confirm armed state via peer-table snapshot.",
    "env": []
  },
  {
    "id": "sitl11-comment",
    "type": "comment",
    "z": "sitl11-tab",
    "name": "Sequential confirm vs broadcast — ack storm vs peer-table armed check",
    "info": "Sequential: paced 200 ms, delivery=confirm, per-vehicle acks on status port.\nBroadcast: single target_system=0 frame; confirm waits on resolved set armed state (peer table), not ack count — inbound ack burst can congest the link.\n\nLaunch five ArduCopter instances:\n  for i in 0 1 2 3 4; do\n    sim_vehicle.py -v ArduCopter -I $i --sysid $((i+1)) \\\n      --out=udp:127.0.0.1:14550 &\n  done\n\nConnection: bind 127.0.0.1:14550, remote 127.0.0.1:14551. Use Snapshot inject after each run to read armed state.",
    "x": 310,
    "y": 40,
    "wires": []
  },
